{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790538951,"nonce":"pdreKe5IL5bBdhSC1IdwRCqq/wM=","title":"AOT walker resolves a bare import to a local file before the built-in module","message":"With hash.wren beside the entry, `import \"hash\" for HashCore` runs the built-in hash module natively (wlift t.wren), but walk_imports resolves \"hash\" to ./hash.wren and compiles that file instead (WLIFT_AOT_DEBUG_IMPORTS shows request_name=hash from disk). A bare name that is a built-in module should resolve to the built-in in an AOT build, as it does natively. A relative \"./hash\" is how a program means the file.","files":null}]}